WEBVTT

1
00:00:34.833 --> 00:00:38.375
THE TROLL PEAKS
ROMSDALEN

2
00:01:04.583 --> 00:01:07.041
Are you coming, Tiny?

3
00:01:07.541 --> 00:01:09.333
Or just gonna hang there all day?

4
00:01:09.416 --> 00:01:11.458
Mind your arthritis, you old fossil.

5
00:01:32.083 --> 00:01:33.166
The Troll Peaks.

6
00:01:35.041 --> 00:01:36.916
Do you remember the fairy tale?

7
00:01:38.083 --> 00:01:40.375
Dad, I don't believe
in fairy tales anymore.

8
00:01:41.208 --> 00:01:42.916
I thought you loved that one.

9
00:01:47.583 --> 00:01:49.875
Once upon a time,
there was a troll wedding.

10
00:01:49.958 --> 00:01:52.375
Thirteen drunk trolls
forgot what time it was,

11
00:01:52.458 --> 00:01:55.083
the sun came up and turned them to stone.

12
00:01:55.166 --> 00:01:56.208
Blah, blah, blah.

13
00:01:57.958 --> 00:01:59.250
You know that there's

14
00:02:00.791 --> 00:02:02.625
an element of truth to all fairy tales.

15
00:02:02.708 --> 00:02:04.041
They're mountain peaks.

16
00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:07.041
You have to see it to believe it.

17
00:02:07.666 --> 00:02:09.041
Isn't that what they say?

18
00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:12.375
It's the other way around.

19
00:02:12.958 --> 00:02:15.125
You have to believe it
to be able to see it.

20
00:02:17.041 --> 00:02:18.500
Can you see them, Nora?

21
00:02:21.458 --> 00:02:23.041
Give it a try. Look.

22
00:02:24.375 --> 00:02:26.041
Not with your eyes.

23
00:02:28.083 --> 00:02:29.125
With your heart.

24
00:02:30.333 --> 00:02:31.500
Believe.

25
00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:13.500
"Made of earth and stone."

26
00:03:16.333 --> 00:03:17.916
"A snow-clad heart."

27
00:03:20.041 --> 00:03:21.375
"And icy bones."

28
00:03:22.875 --> 00:03:24.375
"From darkness they rose."

29
00:03:25.875 --> 00:03:28.416
"And in sunlight they froze."

30
00:03:41.625 --> 00:03:45.625
20 YEARS LATER

31
00:03:46.625 --> 00:03:49.916
THE ATLANTIC COAST
NORTHWESTERN NORWAY

32
00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:58.833
No. Dammit.

33
00:05:44.666 --> 00:05:45.916
Look at you.

34
00:05:46.833 --> 00:05:48.250
Hey there, beautiful.

35
00:05:58.791 --> 00:06:03.458
HJERKINN
DOVRE MOUNTAINS

36
00:06:05.500 --> 00:06:10.291
WE'RE BUILDING THE DOVRE RAILROAD

37
00:06:11.250 --> 00:06:13.166
Let the mountain live!

38
00:06:13.250 --> 00:06:15.833
TO HELL THROUGH A TUNNEL

39
00:06:15.916 --> 00:06:19.666
Let the mountain live!

40
00:06:25.333 --> 00:06:26.875
Bring the explosives.

41
00:06:33.416 --> 00:06:34.416
Everybody out.

42
00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:43.333
Let the mountain live!

43
00:07:11.958 --> 00:07:13.541
Let's get to work, everyone.

44
00:07:29.875 --> 00:07:31.000
Everybody out!

45
00:07:34.583 --> 00:07:35.625
Everybody out!

46
00:07:49.083 --> 00:07:52.416
NORWEGIAN ARMED FORCES OPERATIONAL
HEADQUARTERS, AKERSHUS FORTRESS, OSLO

47
00:07:59.291 --> 00:08:02.333
Receiving reports
of major seismic activity in Dovre.

48
00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:06.250
Where's Sigrid?

49
00:08:10.333 --> 00:08:12.875
Request reconnaissance aircraft
to Dovre Mountains.

50
00:08:12.958 --> 00:08:14.583
Did I miss something?

51
00:08:14.666 --> 00:08:16.875
ØRLAND AIR BASE
TRØNDELAG

52
00:08:19.208 --> 00:08:21.291
<i>This is Raven 4. Ready for takeoff.</i>

53
00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:23.583
<i>Raven 4 is go for takeoff.</i>

54
00:08:31.541 --> 00:08:34.875
<i>HQ, this is Raven 4. Approaching Dovre.</i>

55
00:08:37.208 --> 00:08:38.166
General.

56
00:08:38.250 --> 00:08:39.500
-General.
-Gentlemen.

57
00:08:41.666 --> 00:08:43.833
<i>HQ, are you getting this?</i>

58
00:08:45.750 --> 00:08:46.750
Affirmative.

59
00:08:48.416 --> 00:08:49.583
Alert the government.

60
00:08:50.666 --> 00:08:52.916
THE PRIME MINISTER'S RESIDENCE
OSLO

61
00:08:56.208 --> 00:08:58.291
-Morning.
-Good morning.

62
00:08:58.375 --> 00:09:00.791
-Prime Minister.
-Very formal today, Andreas.

63
00:09:00.875 --> 00:09:03.750
The Minister of Defense
will brief you on the way.

64
00:09:08.541 --> 00:09:10.875
<i>All we have at present are images</i>

65
00:09:10.958 --> 00:09:13.583
<i>from a military reconnaissance aircraft.</i>

66
00:09:13.666 --> 00:09:16.666
Oh my God. It looks like a meteor crater.

67
00:09:16.750 --> 00:09:19.333
<i>A crew is on its way</i>
<i>to assess the situation.</i>

68
00:09:19.416 --> 00:09:20.958
Has word of this got out yet?

69
00:09:21.041 --> 00:09:22.625
<i>I have the media under control.</i>

70
00:09:22.708 --> 00:09:23.750
Do you now?

71
00:09:24.333 --> 00:09:25.541
<i>One more thing.</i>

72
00:09:25.625 --> 00:09:29.833
<i>The aircraft also got footage</i>
<i>of something nearby.</i>

73
00:09:29.916 --> 00:09:32.833
<i>We haven't yet confirmed</i>
<i>whether these indentations</i>

74
00:09:32.916 --> 00:09:34.958
<i>are linked to the event.</i>

75
00:09:35.041 --> 00:09:36.916
<i>-We're working on it.</i>
-Thanks, Fred.

76
00:09:39.166 --> 00:09:40.458
What is that?

77
00:09:41.291 --> 00:09:43.208
Looks like footprints.

78
00:09:46.041 --> 00:09:49.041
I'm not really qualified
to say what it is.

79
00:09:49.125 --> 00:09:50.208
No.

80
00:09:50.291 --> 00:09:52.166
But we need someone who is.

81
00:09:52.750 --> 00:09:55.125
Geologists. Archaeologists. Biologists.

82
00:09:55.208 --> 00:09:57.041
Right. Ologists.

83
00:10:07.750 --> 00:10:09.375
Okay, okay.

84
00:10:38.083 --> 00:10:38.916
Tidemann?

85
00:10:40.250 --> 00:10:41.541
Nora Tidemann?

86
00:10:42.791 --> 00:10:46.208
I have orders
to escort you to Oslo immediately.

87
00:10:46.291 --> 00:10:49.166
-What?
-It's a matter of national security.

88
00:11:04.500 --> 00:11:05.833
-Nora Tidemann?
-Yes.

89
00:11:05.916 --> 00:11:08.750
Andreas Isaksen,
advisor to Prime Minister Moberg.

90
00:11:11.583 --> 00:11:13.833
You guys know I dig up fossils, right?

91
00:11:13.916 --> 00:11:16.541
I don't mean to be so mysterious,
but this is top--

92
00:11:16.625 --> 00:11:18.541
Top secret. They told me already.

93
00:11:20.375 --> 00:11:22.375
You'll be briefed soon.

94
00:11:22.458 --> 00:11:23.958
I heard that too.

95
00:11:24.041 --> 00:11:25.958
Couldn't you have just called?

96
00:11:26.041 --> 00:11:28.250
I think you'll understand.

97
00:11:37.875 --> 00:11:40.458
This isn't exactly
part of the official tour.

98
00:11:44.416 --> 00:11:45.500
<i>Star Trek?</i>

99
00:11:45.583 --> 00:11:48.458
Sigrid and I have this thing.
Not that sort of thi--

100
00:11:48.541 --> 00:11:52.833
You pulled me out of a project
I've spent years financing and planning.

101
00:11:52.916 --> 00:11:56.541
I'm dead tired and starving,
which is a really bad combination.

102
00:11:56.625 --> 00:11:59.125
The reports so far indicate…

103
00:11:59.208 --> 00:12:00.833
And I'm not getting one damn--

104
00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:12.833
Hello.

105
00:12:13.875 --> 00:12:17.416
This is Nora Tidemann.
She's a professor of paleontology.

106
00:12:17.500 --> 00:12:19.375
A paleontologist?

107
00:12:19.458 --> 00:12:20.750
Dinosaurs?

108
00:12:20.833 --> 00:12:22.375
Yes. Or fossils.

109
00:12:25.875 --> 00:12:28.375
Dinosaurs went extinct
65 million years ago.

110
00:12:28.458 --> 00:12:31.750
Then I guess
we'll cross that off our list.

111
00:12:31.833 --> 00:12:33.250
Yes. Please continue, Lunde.

112
00:12:33.333 --> 00:12:35.750
Firstly, let me make it clear

113
00:12:35.833 --> 00:12:40.666
that at this point in time
we cannot safely rule out

114
00:12:40.750 --> 00:12:43.208
a military strike or terrorist attack.

115
00:12:43.291 --> 00:12:45.833
However, reports so far indicate

116
00:12:45.916 --> 00:12:48.833
that the event at Dovre
is of a geological nature.

117
00:12:48.916 --> 00:12:51.000
In addition to the crater,

118
00:12:51.083 --> 00:12:54.291
we've also found
a number of indentations in the terrain.

119
00:12:54.375 --> 00:12:55.875
Karst?

120
00:12:55.958 --> 00:12:57.125
Excuse me?

121
00:12:57.208 --> 00:12:58.416
Sinkholes.

122
00:12:59.166 --> 00:13:01.875
Water trickles down the crevices,

123
00:13:01.958 --> 00:13:05.125
dissolving subterranean lime deposits

124
00:13:05.208 --> 00:13:06.916
until they finally collapse.

125
00:13:07.000 --> 00:13:12.166
It could also be the result
of subterranean gas accumulation.

126
00:13:12.250 --> 00:13:13.416
Yes, methane.

127
00:13:13.500 --> 00:13:16.125
As a consequence of climate change.

128
00:13:16.208 --> 00:13:18.500
We'd better call Greta, then.

129
00:13:19.666 --> 00:13:23.000
The demolition blast
may have caused a chain explosion--

130
00:13:23.083 --> 00:13:25.291
Sorry. Sorry.

131
00:13:27.500 --> 00:13:28.750
Is this a joke?

132
00:13:30.583 --> 00:13:32.000
-Excuse me?
-Is this a joke?

133
00:13:32.500 --> 00:13:35.000
I can assure you
that this is all very real.

134
00:13:37.208 --> 00:13:38.750
Okay. But…

135
00:13:40.458 --> 00:13:42.833
You can see that these are tracks, right?

136
00:13:45.458 --> 00:13:46.333
I mean…

137
00:13:47.000 --> 00:13:48.291
Footprints.

138
00:13:48.375 --> 00:13:51.625
Is there any specific creature

139
00:13:51.708 --> 00:13:53.416
the paleontologist had in mind?

140
00:13:54.666 --> 00:13:58.291
It doesn't really make sense, anyway.
The deepest footprints--

141
00:13:58.375 --> 00:13:59.541
We have something.

142
00:14:00.500 --> 00:14:02.250
One of the protesters

143
00:14:02.333 --> 00:14:04.625
captured the event on their phone.

144
00:14:04.708 --> 00:14:09.541
It wasn't easy to hack.
Nearly impossible, actually.

145
00:14:09.625 --> 00:14:12.333
But I found a back door.
Just had to dig a bit deeper.

146
00:14:13.125 --> 00:14:15.250
Long story short, bingo.

147
00:14:15.333 --> 00:14:18.208
<i>Let the mountain live!</i>

148
00:14:18.291 --> 00:14:22.500
<i>Let the mountain live! Let the…</i>

149
00:14:27.208 --> 00:14:28.291
<i>Oh my God.</i>

150
00:14:55.125 --> 00:14:57.916
So what exactly do we have up there?

151
00:14:59.500 --> 00:15:01.291
Hey, Sigrid?

152
00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:05.458
Could you go back a bit in the video?

153
00:15:10.041 --> 00:15:11.750
Can you play it from there?

154
00:15:11.833 --> 00:15:13.958
<i>Let the mountain live. Let the…</i>

155
00:15:17.708 --> 00:15:19.375
It sounds like…

156
00:15:21.583 --> 00:15:22.541
an animal.

157
00:15:26.875 --> 00:15:27.708
Stop.

158
00:16:04.041 --> 00:16:06.166
<i>The mountain pass over Dovre is closed</i>

159
00:16:06.250 --> 00:16:08.958
<i>due to work</i>
<i>on the new high-speed railroad.</i>

160
00:16:09.041 --> 00:16:11.583
<i>The route will reopen soon.</i>

161
00:16:11.666 --> 00:16:13.541
I don't know what's up with Solo.

162
00:16:14.208 --> 00:16:15.666
He's going mad out there.

163
00:16:18.291 --> 00:16:19.125
Oh well.

164
00:16:42.375 --> 00:16:43.416
Oddrun.

165
00:16:43.500 --> 00:16:44.833
What is that?

166
00:16:57.875 --> 00:16:59.541
Oddrun, into the basement!

167
00:17:00.375 --> 00:17:01.583
Come on.

168
00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:50.500
Are you claiming it's related to us?

169
00:17:50.583 --> 00:17:52.416
Morphologically speaking.

170
00:17:52.500 --> 00:17:54.333
Please use words

171
00:17:54.416 --> 00:17:56.958
that normal people can understand.

172
00:17:57.041 --> 00:17:58.833
As far as I can tell,

173
00:17:58.916 --> 00:18:01.541
we have two legs and two arms.

174
00:18:01.625 --> 00:18:04.708
What are you suggesting, miss?
That it's some kind of giant?

175
00:18:04.791 --> 00:18:06.833
King Kong, perhaps?

176
00:18:06.916 --> 00:18:08.916
The biggest primates we know of

177
00:18:09.541 --> 00:18:12.708
are believed to have been
four meters tall.

178
00:18:12.791 --> 00:18:16.208
This seems more like 40 or 50.

179
00:18:16.750 --> 00:18:18.208
Which is unnatural.

180
00:18:18.291 --> 00:18:19.666
Or supernatural.

181
00:18:24.208 --> 00:18:25.416
Are there

182
00:18:26.375 --> 00:18:27.708
any other findings?

183
00:18:28.250 --> 00:18:30.458
Our searches have so far proved fruitless.

184
00:18:30.541 --> 00:18:32.125
So what's the plan here?

185
00:18:34.000 --> 00:18:37.291
Sit here and discuss theories,
or actually do something?

186
00:18:37.375 --> 00:18:39.291
Miss, please.

187
00:18:42.458 --> 00:18:44.500
That's Professor Tidemann.

188
00:18:45.416 --> 00:18:47.916
I'm willing to put my work on hold

189
00:18:49.041 --> 00:18:51.250
to help out at Dovre if needed.

190
00:18:52.625 --> 00:18:56.541
I don't want to waste time discussing
gas deposits with Professor Sinkhole.

191
00:19:07.791 --> 00:19:08.708
Tidemann.

192
00:19:10.291 --> 00:19:12.583
You've been made a scientific advisor.

193
00:19:13.166 --> 00:19:15.666
There's been an event in Lesja.
We need to go now.

194
00:19:15.750 --> 00:19:16.666
We?

195
00:19:18.250 --> 00:19:20.458
I've been assigned to look after you.

196
00:19:42.583 --> 00:19:46.791
What made you start digging for fossils?

197
00:19:49.708 --> 00:19:53.541
I've always been fond of nature.

198
00:19:54.041 --> 00:19:57.333
I was brought up
on fairy tales and stories and stuff.

199
00:19:57.416 --> 00:20:00.666
My dad was a professor of folklore.

200
00:20:00.750 --> 00:20:03.625
A folklorist? I thought they were extinct.

201
00:20:05.375 --> 00:20:07.458
What about your mother?

202
00:20:07.541 --> 00:20:09.125
She died when I was ten.

203
00:20:09.625 --> 00:20:10.458
Sorry?

204
00:20:10.541 --> 00:20:11.958
She died when I was ten.

205
00:20:17.125 --> 00:20:21.166
It's nice that you two had each other.
You and your father.

206
00:20:25.666 --> 00:20:26.541
Yeah.

207
00:20:26.625 --> 00:20:27.625
What?

208
00:20:28.541 --> 00:20:30.208
My dad had a big heart

209
00:20:30.291 --> 00:20:33.083
and an even bigger imagination.

210
00:20:34.291 --> 00:20:37.375
He kind of lost touch with reality
after a while.

211
00:20:37.458 --> 00:20:38.291
Yeah?

212
00:20:40.916 --> 00:20:44.000
"You have to believe it
to be able to see it," he used to say.

213
00:20:46.166 --> 00:20:49.666
I guess he believed a bit too much.

214
00:20:50.250 --> 00:20:51.083
Yeah.

215
00:20:53.500 --> 00:20:54.958
I wanted to be a writer.

216
00:20:57.083 --> 00:21:00.166
I'm writing this book about a monk

217
00:21:00.250 --> 00:21:03.625
who can pull his head off,
throw it at bad guys and bite them.

218
00:21:03.708 --> 00:21:05.083
Oh my God.

219
00:21:06.541 --> 00:21:09.833
Right? And use his fingers as darts.

220
00:21:30.333 --> 00:21:31.625
Professor Tidemann?

221
00:21:32.208 --> 00:21:33.041
Nora.

222
00:21:33.125 --> 00:21:35.291
Captain Holm, Special Operations Forces.

223
00:21:35.375 --> 00:21:38.583
-Andreas Isaksen, Prime Minister's Office.
-Welcome to Lesja.

224
00:21:42.166 --> 00:21:43.333
Here's the situation.

225
00:21:43.416 --> 00:21:45.625
Something came from that direction,

226
00:21:45.708 --> 00:21:49.083
went through here,
and continued down the valley.

227
00:21:49.750 --> 00:21:53.875
The tracks come to a stop
20 klicks south of here in the mountains.

228
00:21:53.958 --> 00:21:55.250
-A complete stop?
-Yes.

229
00:21:57.583 --> 00:21:59.125
Any other sightings?

230
00:21:59.208 --> 00:22:01.250
No. We've searched the whole area.

231
00:22:01.333 --> 00:22:02.333
Nothing.

232
00:22:04.500 --> 00:22:07.375
-You're a paleontologist?
-Majored in paleobiology.

233
00:22:07.458 --> 00:22:08.708
I see.

234
00:22:09.625 --> 00:22:11.833
So what's your theory?

235
00:22:12.500 --> 00:22:15.166
There's a T. rex on the loose
in the mountains?

236
00:22:15.250 --> 00:22:17.875
That remains to be seen, Captain Holm.

237
00:22:17.958 --> 00:22:18.791
Kris.

238
00:22:20.333 --> 00:22:21.333
Call me Kris.

239
00:22:22.166 --> 00:22:23.166
Captain Kris?

240
00:22:23.875 --> 00:22:24.791
Yeah.

241
00:22:26.250 --> 00:22:29.416
I… couldn't see much.

242
00:22:30.333 --> 00:22:31.375
It was dark.

243
00:22:33.125 --> 00:22:37.833
Was it dark because it was cloudy?

244
00:22:38.583 --> 00:22:40.500
No. It was something else.

245
00:22:41.583 --> 00:22:44.750
It was as if we were
in the shadow of the mountain.

246
00:22:46.666 --> 00:22:48.541
And the mountain was moving.

247
00:22:50.583 --> 00:22:52.750
Solo thought it was horrible too.

248
00:22:53.333 --> 00:22:54.541
Didn't you, boy?

249
00:22:54.625 --> 00:22:56.333
Yes, you did.

250
00:22:57.250 --> 00:22:59.916
Did you notice anything else?

251
00:23:01.583 --> 00:23:04.208
Can you think of anything at all?

252
00:23:04.291 --> 00:23:07.791
I'm sorry. I'm still a bit shaken.

253
00:23:08.375 --> 00:23:09.291
That's okay.

254
00:23:12.000 --> 00:23:13.208
Thank you very much.

255
00:23:14.666 --> 00:23:16.041
There was one thing.

256
00:23:18.000 --> 00:23:19.583
It was like…

257
00:23:21.083 --> 00:23:23.708
a kind of howling.

258
00:23:23.791 --> 00:23:26.875
What are you talking about?
I didn't hear any howling.

259
00:23:27.458 --> 00:23:30.250
He can't hear things like that.
He has a hearing aid.

260
00:23:30.333 --> 00:23:31.208
What?

261
00:23:31.291 --> 00:23:34.375
Howling? Like the wind?

262
00:23:34.458 --> 00:23:37.583
No. It was more like a melody.

263
00:23:38.666 --> 00:23:40.166
A sorrowful melody.

264
00:23:41.500 --> 00:23:43.208
It made me terribly sad.

265
00:24:02.416 --> 00:24:05.791
It's as if a force of nature
wreaked havoc through the valley.

266
00:24:06.791 --> 00:24:08.666
A two-legged force of nature.

267
00:24:20.291 --> 00:24:21.375
Do you notice that?

268
00:24:22.750 --> 00:24:23.666
What?

269
00:24:24.833 --> 00:24:26.000
That smell.

270
00:24:27.416 --> 00:24:28.500
Norwegian nature?

271
00:24:29.500 --> 00:24:30.333
Yeah.

272
00:24:30.916 --> 00:24:31.958
But there's…

273
00:24:33.958 --> 00:24:34.791
more.

274
00:24:35.416 --> 00:24:36.750
More nature?

275
00:24:36.833 --> 00:24:38.916
Yeah. Hypernature.

276
00:24:39.000 --> 00:24:41.375
HYPERNATURE

277
00:24:41.458 --> 00:24:42.791
"Hypernature."

278
00:24:47.750 --> 00:24:49.125
Look how deep it is.

279
00:24:58.583 --> 00:25:00.666
-What are you doing?
-UV light.

280
00:25:00.750 --> 00:25:02.541
Checking for biological traces.

281
00:25:04.791 --> 00:25:05.833
See anything?

282
00:25:07.625 --> 00:25:10.500
Nope. Just earth and stone.

283
00:25:14.708 --> 00:25:16.666
-What is it?
-It's just…

284
00:25:18.333 --> 00:25:19.875
Just an old rhyme.

285
00:25:21.750 --> 00:25:23.166
Is there a plan?

286
00:25:25.041 --> 00:25:26.041
Thoughts?

287
00:25:32.750 --> 00:25:34.875
You said it was 20 kilometers south?

288
00:25:44.000 --> 00:25:45.250
They end here.

289
00:25:47.000 --> 00:25:48.083
No more tracks.

290
00:25:50.333 --> 00:25:53.583
As you can see on the thermal scanner,
there are no signs of life.

291
00:25:54.250 --> 00:25:55.666
Nothing but mountain.

292
00:25:58.666 --> 00:26:01.083
Something this big can't just disappear.

293
00:26:01.166 --> 00:26:02.625
It can't hide either.

294
00:26:14.208 --> 00:26:16.916
CAMOUFLAGE?

295
00:26:17.000 --> 00:26:18.166
What do you think?

296
00:26:26.166 --> 00:26:27.375
Dammit!

297
00:26:27.458 --> 00:26:29.000
-What is it?
-We…

298
00:26:29.875 --> 00:26:31.875
We have to pay someone a visit.

299
00:26:40.083 --> 00:26:41.041
Listen.

300
00:26:41.125 --> 00:26:43.583
Let me do the talking.

301
00:26:45.083 --> 00:26:46.250
I'm staying here!

302
00:26:47.083 --> 00:26:48.333
I'm not going back!

303
00:26:49.791 --> 00:26:51.500
We're not taking you anywhere.

304
00:26:52.500 --> 00:26:54.041
Put the shotgun down, Dad.

305
00:26:58.250 --> 00:26:59.250
Tiny?

306
00:27:04.583 --> 00:27:06.041
Can you put the shotgun down?

307
00:27:14.291 --> 00:27:15.416
It's been a while.

308
00:27:18.958 --> 00:27:20.666
Yeah. I've been busy.

309
00:27:25.708 --> 00:27:26.750
Who's the suit?

310
00:27:28.708 --> 00:27:30.166
Andreas Isaksen.

311
00:27:30.250 --> 00:27:32.333
Advisor to Prime Minister Moberg.

312
00:27:33.958 --> 00:27:34.791
Yeah.

313
00:27:34.875 --> 00:27:36.333
-Everything okay?
-Hey!

314
00:27:36.416 --> 00:27:37.541
Whoa!

315
00:27:37.625 --> 00:27:39.041
Hey!

316
00:27:39.125 --> 00:27:40.166
Calm down.

317
00:27:41.333 --> 00:27:44.125
This is Captain Kris… toffer Holm.

318
00:27:44.750 --> 00:27:46.500
This is Tobias Tidemann.

319
00:27:46.583 --> 00:27:48.083
He's her dad.

320
00:27:50.083 --> 00:27:50.958
Okay.

321
00:27:54.416 --> 00:27:55.250
Hi.

322
00:27:56.208 --> 00:27:57.500
Can we go inside?

323
00:27:58.625 --> 00:28:00.166
Just to talk?

324
00:28:04.708 --> 00:28:05.750
And, Dad.

325
00:28:07.583 --> 00:28:10.000
Can you please put some pants on?

326
00:28:29.416 --> 00:28:31.041
You've done the place up, I see.

327
00:28:32.708 --> 00:28:33.541
No.

328
00:28:42.416 --> 00:28:43.833
The winter of 1943.

329
00:28:44.750 --> 00:28:47.541
The Nazis used Russian POWs
to build the Nordland line,

330
00:28:47.625 --> 00:28:49.375
but they only got as far as Bodø.

331
00:28:49.958 --> 00:28:52.458
Some believe construction was halted

332
00:28:53.208 --> 00:28:55.416
because of something in the mountain.

333
00:28:55.500 --> 00:28:57.083
Really? What did they find?

334
00:28:57.166 --> 00:28:58.333
Something came out.

335
00:28:58.416 --> 00:29:02.000
Exactly, but it was hard to prove.
They hushed it up.

336
00:29:02.083 --> 00:29:03.500
Got rid of the evidence.

337
00:29:03.583 --> 00:29:04.833
No, Dad.

338
00:29:04.916 --> 00:29:05.875
Today.

339
00:29:07.875 --> 00:29:10.083
Something came out of the mountain today.

340
00:29:28.541 --> 00:29:31.958
We've tracked the footprints

341
00:29:32.041 --> 00:29:33.708
of whatever this thing is,

342
00:29:33.791 --> 00:29:34.958
but they just stop.

343
00:29:37.750 --> 00:29:41.250
No superstition, fairy tales, fantasy,
or anything like that.

344
00:29:41.333 --> 00:29:43.250
We're done with that.

345
00:29:44.708 --> 00:29:47.625
I just thought there might be
something in your work

346
00:29:47.708 --> 00:29:49.875
that could steer us
in the right direction.

347
00:29:51.000 --> 00:29:53.666
You know these mountains
better than anyone.

348
00:30:01.250 --> 00:30:04.166
Did you know Norway imposed
the maximum penalty

349
00:30:04.250 --> 00:30:07.416
for having contact with trolls
right up until 1840?

350
00:30:07.500 --> 00:30:08.500
Trolls?

351
00:30:09.416 --> 00:30:12.250
What if I told you
that a thousand years ago

352
00:30:12.333 --> 00:30:14.791
trolls roamed all over Norway?

353
00:30:14.875 --> 00:30:17.375
I'm not having this discussion again.

354
00:30:17.458 --> 00:30:19.333
You know as well as I do

355
00:30:19.416 --> 00:30:22.166
that a thousand years is nothing
in evolutionary terms.

356
00:30:22.250 --> 00:30:23.833
If they were real,

357
00:30:23.916 --> 00:30:27.375
we'd have extracted DNA
from troll fossils long ago.

358
00:30:27.458 --> 00:30:29.833
We'd know what made them extinct.

359
00:30:29.916 --> 00:30:33.000
We do know what made them extinct.

360
00:30:34.416 --> 00:30:36.000
The Christianization of Norway.

361
00:30:38.000 --> 00:30:40.750
And why is it you're the only person
who knows this?

362
00:30:40.833 --> 00:30:44.833
Because I was this close to exposing them
when they locked me up.

363
00:30:45.500 --> 00:30:48.458
Someone has always known something.
For God's sake.

364
00:30:49.583 --> 00:30:52.125
What did Kittelsen know?

365
00:30:53.083 --> 00:30:55.625
Did he make this obvious mistake
on purpose?

366
00:30:55.708 --> 00:30:57.375
-Mistake?
-Please.

367
00:30:57.458 --> 00:30:59.375
The collection of folk tales.

368
00:30:59.458 --> 00:31:01.750
All the myths and artwork.

369
00:31:01.833 --> 00:31:04.125
-All meant to cover up the truth.
-Dad!

370
00:31:04.208 --> 00:31:07.625
Every recorded fairy tale
was designed to tarnish their legacy.

371
00:31:07.708 --> 00:31:10.875
To make fun of them.
Thank Asbjørnsen and Moe for that.

372
00:31:10.958 --> 00:31:14.166
They're portrayed as dumb, evil, miserly,

373
00:31:14.250 --> 00:31:18.958
while humans are made out
to be mentally superior.

374
00:31:19.041 --> 00:31:22.166
Repeat a lie often enough,
and it becomes the truth.

375
00:31:22.250 --> 00:31:24.416
A politician who's figured it out.

376
00:31:24.500 --> 00:31:25.583
That's new.

377
00:31:28.333 --> 00:31:30.791
Let's take a two-minute time-out.

378
00:31:30.875 --> 00:31:32.916
-Good idea.
-Two minutes?

379
00:31:33.000 --> 00:31:34.458
We can't waste time.

380
00:31:34.541 --> 00:31:36.625
-We need to go, Tiny.
-Don't call me that.

381
00:31:37.208 --> 00:31:39.458
Adventure awaits. Mind your head.

382
00:31:43.166 --> 00:31:44.500
<i>They stop here.</i>

383
00:31:46.791 --> 00:31:48.791
We're here, right?

384
00:31:50.000 --> 00:31:51.500
Affirmative.

385
00:31:51.583 --> 00:31:52.541
Yeah.

386
00:31:55.041 --> 00:31:58.458
That means he walked from there
all the way here.

387
00:31:59.333 --> 00:32:00.166
He?

388
00:32:01.000 --> 00:32:03.125
It could be a <i>gýgr</i>, of course.

389
00:32:04.000 --> 00:32:04.833
<i>Gýgr</i>?

390
00:32:07.083 --> 00:32:08.000
A troll hag.

391
00:32:10.083 --> 00:32:11.375
A female troll.

392
00:32:13.708 --> 00:32:15.333
Jesus Christ.

393
00:32:18.583 --> 00:32:20.000
Wait! Down!

394
00:32:21.875 --> 00:32:22.791
Go down!

395
00:32:23.541 --> 00:32:24.708
Go down here!

396
00:32:31.333 --> 00:32:32.833
The Tidemanns.

397
00:32:34.708 --> 00:32:36.250
Now there's a peculiar bunch.

398
00:32:39.500 --> 00:32:42.916
He's always been a bit eccentric.

399
00:32:43.458 --> 00:32:47.041
And at some point,
he fell down this rabbit hole.

400
00:32:48.500 --> 00:32:50.125
Lost his job.

401
00:32:50.208 --> 00:32:52.041
Was committed for a while.

402
00:32:53.375 --> 00:32:54.208
I see.

403
00:32:55.166 --> 00:32:57.958
I just thought
he'd be in a better state by now.

404
00:33:03.666 --> 00:33:06.208
I think I'd better…

405
00:33:06.291 --> 00:33:07.833
-You do that.
-Good idea.

406
00:33:12.500 --> 00:33:13.958
Found anything?

407
00:33:15.000 --> 00:33:17.083
It's wrong. Everything is wrong here.

408
00:33:17.166 --> 00:33:18.875
-What?
-The map.

409
00:33:20.208 --> 00:33:22.416
The topography is all topsy-turvy.

410
00:33:22.500 --> 00:33:24.041
Everything is off.

411
00:33:24.125 --> 00:33:24.958
See?

412
00:33:31.541 --> 00:33:32.625
What?

413
00:33:33.583 --> 00:33:37.833
Look at us, Tiny.
Adventuring. Just like the old days.

414
00:33:37.916 --> 00:33:40.000
This isn't a reconciliation thing.

415
00:33:40.583 --> 00:33:41.750
Just so you know.

416
00:33:43.291 --> 00:33:44.708
Your eyes used to sparkle

417
00:33:44.791 --> 00:33:47.125
when I told you
about the secrets of the world.

418
00:33:48.375 --> 00:33:49.916
Just as curious as your mom.

419
00:33:52.291 --> 00:33:53.291
What happened?

420
00:33:54.458 --> 00:33:56.708
-I grew up.
-Come on.

421
00:33:58.416 --> 00:34:00.833
What do you think we're looking for here?

422
00:34:02.250 --> 00:34:04.375
What you're suggesting is pure fantasy.

423
00:34:04.458 --> 00:34:07.708
Dinosaurs were considered
imaginary beings as well.

424
00:34:07.791 --> 00:34:10.500
-It's unnatural.
-No, it is nature.

425
00:34:10.583 --> 00:34:13.125
-For God's sake.
-Made of earth and stone.

426
00:34:14.500 --> 00:34:17.041
From mountains they came,
risen from the ground.

427
00:34:19.458 --> 00:34:21.083
-What is it?
-That smell.

428
00:34:23.541 --> 00:34:25.041
I bathe every Saturday.

429
00:34:25.125 --> 00:34:26.125
No.

430
00:34:27.583 --> 00:34:28.750
It's hypernature.

431
00:34:30.500 --> 00:34:31.500
Hypernature?

432
00:34:33.916 --> 00:34:35.000
Hypernature.

433
00:34:39.166 --> 00:34:41.583
HYPERNATURE
CAMOUFLAGE?

434
00:34:52.083 --> 00:34:52.916
Dad.

435
00:35:06.166 --> 00:35:07.000
Kris.

436
00:35:16.125 --> 00:35:16.958
Start it up.

437
00:35:30.291 --> 00:35:31.125
Come on!

438
00:35:35.416 --> 00:35:36.333
Come on!

439
00:35:58.541 --> 00:35:59.833
Contact Oslo!

440
00:36:00.666 --> 00:36:02.666
Putting it on screen now.

441
00:36:11.333 --> 00:36:12.541
You need to see this.

442
00:36:21.208 --> 00:36:23.625
What on earth is that?

443
00:36:33.458 --> 00:36:36.666
RENA MILITARY CAMP
ØSTERDALEN

444
00:36:37.416 --> 00:36:38.833
Pretty intense, huh?

445
00:36:38.916 --> 00:36:41.458
-Even the suit's jazzed.
-Yes, it's big.

446
00:36:42.125 --> 00:36:44.833
Dad, no matter what they ask,

447
00:36:45.541 --> 00:36:47.500
no matter what the uniforms say,

448
00:36:47.583 --> 00:36:50.041
don't mention the word "troll," okay?

449
00:36:50.875 --> 00:36:52.958
<i>"Troll"? What do you mean, </i>"<i>troll"?</i>

450
00:36:53.041 --> 00:36:54.166
Is the sound bad--

451
00:36:54.250 --> 00:36:56.375
He doesn't mean a fairy tale creature.

452
00:36:56.458 --> 00:36:57.625
Troll.

453
00:36:57.708 --> 00:36:59.625
It's a troll!

454
00:37:00.125 --> 00:37:01.083
I'm sorry.

455
00:37:01.708 --> 00:37:03.500
The point is that we won't know

456
00:37:03.583 --> 00:37:07.250
what kind of creature it is
until we can study it over time.

457
00:37:07.333 --> 00:37:09.958
<i>Time? We can't afford to wait.</i>

458
00:37:10.041 --> 00:37:13.250
We can't afford
to make rash decisions either.

459
00:37:13.333 --> 00:37:16.250
<i>What do you suggest then?</i>
<i>An eating contest?</i>

460
00:37:16.333 --> 00:37:20.208
<i>-Like in the fairy tale?</i>
-If I may.

461
00:37:20.291 --> 00:37:22.166
You're not exactly all there

462
00:37:22.250 --> 00:37:25.458
if you choose to build a railroad
through the Dovre Mountains.

463
00:37:25.541 --> 00:37:27.500
-Dad.
-It's mocking nature.

464
00:37:27.583 --> 00:37:30.625
But you did it because you could.

465
00:37:30.708 --> 00:37:32.958
You never stop to think
whether you should.

466
00:37:33.041 --> 00:37:34.541
-What are you doing?
-Helping.

467
00:37:34.625 --> 00:37:36.875
No. This is my PTA meetings all over…

468
00:37:36.958 --> 00:37:39.000
<i>-Are we done?</i>
-Your dimwit teacher…

469
00:37:39.083 --> 00:37:40.291
If I may…

470
00:37:40.375 --> 00:37:44.083
This isn't some goblin.
This is a full-grown mountain troll.

471
00:37:44.166 --> 00:37:45.208
<i>Get him out.</i>

472
00:37:45.291 --> 00:37:47.583
-Twenty years of research.
<i>-Now!</i>

473
00:37:47.666 --> 00:37:50.041
And I'm the crazy one?

474
00:37:50.125 --> 00:37:52.291
-I'll take care of it.
-Good luck with that.

475
00:37:53.416 --> 00:37:54.500
Please!

476
00:37:55.125 --> 00:37:57.000
I know how to walk.

477
00:37:57.083 --> 00:37:58.208
Prime Minister.

478
00:37:59.041 --> 00:38:01.708
All we're asking for
is a little more time.

479
00:38:01.791 --> 00:38:04.875
<i>I'm sorry, Tidemann. The risk is too high.</i>

480
00:38:04.958 --> 00:38:07.083
<i>We need to leave this to the Armed Forces.</i>

481
00:38:12.041 --> 00:38:14.458
You insist on your fairy tale theories,

482
00:38:14.541 --> 00:38:17.708
but this isn't some mystical creature

483
00:38:17.791 --> 00:38:21.041
that can smell Christian blood
and turns to stone in the sun.

484
00:38:21.125 --> 00:38:23.625
If you're so sure, why did you come to me?

485
00:38:28.083 --> 00:38:30.375
This fairy tale's over anyway.

486
00:38:30.458 --> 00:38:31.958
I'm going back to my work.

487
00:38:33.083 --> 00:38:34.208
Nice to see you, Dad.

488
00:38:34.291 --> 00:38:37.125
Imagine waking up one day,
and everything you know is gone.

489
00:38:38.625 --> 00:38:40.500
You wake up to a whole new world.

490
00:38:42.750 --> 00:38:43.875
And this troll…

491
00:38:46.666 --> 00:38:47.500
This creature.

492
00:38:50.208 --> 00:38:52.083
You think it wants to be here?

493
00:38:53.958 --> 00:38:55.958
We can scare it with weapons.

494
00:38:56.041 --> 00:38:57.750
Push it around.

495
00:38:57.833 --> 00:39:00.750
But I promise you, Nora.
Nature will push back.

496
00:39:04.541 --> 00:39:06.916
What do you want us to do? Give up?

497
00:39:07.000 --> 00:39:08.916
Even the suit doesn't want to give up.

498
00:39:10.125 --> 00:39:11.416
No…

499
00:39:16.625 --> 00:39:18.541
This adventure is just starting.

500
00:39:29.541 --> 00:39:30.583
There you are.

501
00:39:32.500 --> 00:39:33.333
Kris.

502
00:39:34.166 --> 00:39:35.166
Wait!

503
00:39:36.166 --> 00:39:39.375
You're civilians, Tidemann.
This is a military operation.

504
00:39:39.458 --> 00:39:42.708
I didn't realize we were back on
a last-name basis, Captain Holm.

505
00:39:42.791 --> 00:39:45.625
We won't get in the way.
We'll just observe.

506
00:39:46.208 --> 00:39:48.208
You won't even notice we're here.

507
00:39:48.791 --> 00:39:50.666
-Watch where you're going!
-Sorry.

508
00:39:50.750 --> 00:39:52.375
Out of the question.

509
00:39:53.083 --> 00:39:56.541
Sometimes you have to
bend the rules a little, right?

510
00:39:58.750 --> 00:39:59.583
Kris.

511
00:40:00.208 --> 00:40:01.208
Please.

512
00:40:03.666 --> 00:40:04.500
Tidemann.

513
00:40:05.083 --> 00:40:05.916
-Yes?
-Yeah?

514
00:40:06.500 --> 00:40:10.458
If you're coming, you stay
in the background and follow orders.

515
00:40:11.041 --> 00:40:12.041
Understood?

516
00:40:14.000 --> 00:40:16.791
-If Oslo finds out I brought you…
-They won't.

517
00:40:17.458 --> 00:40:19.833
Don't worry. You'll be dead before sunup.

518
00:40:41.750 --> 00:40:42.625
<i>Let's go!</i>

519
00:41:10.458 --> 00:41:11.916
Ladies and gentlemen,

520
00:41:12.000 --> 00:41:13.875
we're live from Heidal.

521
00:41:16.750 --> 00:41:18.333
<i>Piranha, this is Viking.</i>

522
00:41:18.416 --> 00:41:20.000
What's your status? Over.

523
00:41:20.083 --> 00:41:22.750
Viking, this is Piranha.
We are in position.

524
00:41:22.833 --> 00:41:25.375
<i>3-Alpha, status? Over.</i>

525
00:41:27.083 --> 00:41:30.333
<i>Viking, this is 3-Alpha.</i>
<i>We are in position. Over.</i>

526
00:41:30.416 --> 00:41:31.250
Copy.

527
00:41:36.375 --> 00:41:37.500
What happens now?

528
00:41:38.916 --> 00:41:40.125
We wait.

529
00:41:42.833 --> 00:41:46.625
So if I've got this right,
he can remove his own head?

530
00:41:46.708 --> 00:41:47.791
Yeah.

531
00:41:47.875 --> 00:41:50.125
Throw it at people and bite them?

532
00:41:50.208 --> 00:41:51.416
Yes, or his hand.

533
00:41:51.500 --> 00:41:55.541
He can rip it off
and throw it like a snowball fist.

534
00:41:57.041 --> 00:41:58.541
Fascinating.

535
00:42:19.666 --> 00:42:20.958
Can you picture them?

536
00:42:23.375 --> 00:42:25.708
Wandering around in herds.

537
00:42:27.000 --> 00:42:28.041
Whole families.

538
00:42:30.041 --> 00:42:32.000
"Made of earth and stone."

539
00:42:32.083 --> 00:42:34.083
"A snow-clad heart and icy bones."

540
00:42:40.458 --> 00:42:41.791
I remember all that.

541
00:42:45.083 --> 00:42:47.208
All the fairy tales you and Mom told me.

542
00:42:48.208 --> 00:42:49.041
And

543
00:42:49.916 --> 00:42:51.375
the emptiness afterwards.

544
00:42:54.833 --> 00:42:56.708
But I also remember

545
00:42:58.041 --> 00:43:00.000
what filled that void.

546
00:43:02.583 --> 00:43:04.458
The adventures of Tiny and Big.

547
00:43:09.083 --> 00:43:11.375
Are we having a reconciliation thing here?

548
00:43:12.416 --> 00:43:13.333
You and I?

549
00:43:25.041 --> 00:43:26.708
Is that a PVS-31?

550
00:43:27.500 --> 00:43:29.166
It is, actually.

551
00:43:29.791 --> 00:43:31.750
I thought as much.

552
00:43:31.833 --> 00:43:33.833
-You have military experience?
-Some.

553
00:43:34.583 --> 00:43:35.416
Yeah?

554
00:43:36.041 --> 00:43:37.041
<i>Call of Duty.</i>

555
00:43:41.833 --> 00:43:43.208
You know, Nora.

556
00:43:45.375 --> 00:43:46.541
You lost us both

557
00:43:47.250 --> 00:43:48.708
the day your mother died.

558
00:43:54.875 --> 00:43:55.875
You're here now.

559
00:43:59.041 --> 00:44:00.041
You old fossil.

560
00:44:04.583 --> 00:44:06.041
Are you crying?

561
00:44:07.458 --> 00:44:09.250
Must be my pine allergy.

562
00:44:11.083 --> 00:44:12.666
Forests give me a reaction.

563
00:44:25.291 --> 00:44:26.375
Impressive, huh?

564
00:44:26.458 --> 00:44:28.958
Gives you a real arcade feeling.

565
00:44:29.625 --> 00:44:32.208
<i>3-Alpha calling Viking. Over.</i>

566
00:44:32.291 --> 00:44:33.541
This is Viking.

567
00:44:35.875 --> 00:44:37.500
Copy. I need the helmet.

568
00:44:37.583 --> 00:44:39.291
Just loosen the strap.

569
00:44:39.791 --> 00:44:40.666
Okay.

570
00:44:40.750 --> 00:44:43.375
Move your greasy fingers.

571
00:44:46.333 --> 00:44:47.208
He's here.

572
00:45:01.458 --> 00:45:02.541
Can I see?

573
00:45:14.791 --> 00:45:15.958
It's stopped.

574
00:45:16.791 --> 00:45:18.625
He knows we're here.

575
00:45:21.500 --> 00:45:23.916
Oslo, this is Viking. Awaiting orders.

576
00:45:25.375 --> 00:45:26.250
Viking.

577
00:45:27.500 --> 00:45:29.666
You have permission to open fire.

578
00:45:32.500 --> 00:45:33.875
3-Alpha, this is Viking.

579
00:45:35.083 --> 00:45:36.166
Launch attack.

580
00:45:37.125 --> 00:45:39.041
Roger. Open fire!

581
00:45:39.125 --> 00:45:40.208
Idiots.

582
00:45:55.166 --> 00:45:57.375
-It's not working.
-You're just agitating it.

583
00:45:57.458 --> 00:45:59.875
3-Alpha, pull back!

584
00:46:03.708 --> 00:46:06.125
Piranha, open fire! I repeat, open fire!

585
00:46:06.208 --> 00:46:08.666
<i>Roger, Viking. 9-8.</i>

586
00:46:08.750 --> 00:46:09.791
Fire!

587
00:46:09.875 --> 00:46:12.333
Take cover! Incoming artillery!

588
00:46:47.666 --> 00:46:49.208
Pull back.

589
00:46:49.875 --> 00:46:50.958
Pull back!

590
00:47:04.541 --> 00:47:05.791
Pull out!

591
00:47:06.458 --> 00:47:07.750
Pull out!

592
00:47:08.250 --> 00:47:09.416
Go!

593
00:47:17.333 --> 00:47:18.166
Over here!

594
00:47:34.333 --> 00:47:35.958
Hallowed be thy name.

595
00:47:37.083 --> 00:47:38.375
Thy kingdom come.

596
00:47:41.000 --> 00:47:42.333
Forgive us our trespasses…

597
00:47:45.708 --> 00:47:48.416
as we forgive those
who trespass against us.

598
00:47:49.916 --> 00:47:52.541
For thine is the kingdom, the power

599
00:47:53.208 --> 00:47:55.291
and the glory. Forever.

600
00:47:57.500 --> 00:47:58.375
Amen.

601
00:48:02.458 --> 00:48:04.208
-We're getting you out.
-Kris!

602
00:48:17.625 --> 00:48:18.625
The blood, Nora.

603
00:48:22.458 --> 00:48:24.083
He could smell his blood.

604
00:48:25.208 --> 00:48:26.958
We have to keep moving. Come on.

605
00:48:28.708 --> 00:48:30.083
-Hey!
-Dad!

606
00:48:31.416 --> 00:48:32.875
There, there.

607
00:48:33.375 --> 00:48:34.250
Listen.

608
00:48:37.750 --> 00:48:40.250
There, there.

609
00:48:47.291 --> 00:48:48.791
There, there.

610
00:48:54.000 --> 00:48:54.833
Easy.

611
00:48:57.625 --> 00:48:58.833
Easy.

612
00:49:01.541 --> 00:49:02.541
There we go.

613
00:49:45.250 --> 00:49:47.416
Dad!

614
00:50:00.916 --> 00:50:01.750
Dad?

615
00:50:08.666 --> 00:50:10.166
-Nora.
-Are you okay?

616
00:50:28.208 --> 00:50:30.125
Don't move. Help is on the way.

617
00:50:32.375 --> 00:50:34.375
Nora, did you see?

618
00:50:35.333 --> 00:50:37.541
-Shush. Don't speak.
-You saw.

619
00:50:43.333 --> 00:50:44.208
The palace.

620
00:50:47.666 --> 00:50:48.583
The king.

621
00:50:51.583 --> 00:50:52.708
Home.

622
00:50:55.625 --> 00:50:56.458
My girl.

623
00:50:59.333 --> 00:51:00.250
Believe.

624
00:51:22.541 --> 00:51:23.375
Dad?

625
00:51:26.708 --> 00:51:27.583
Dad?

626
00:51:29.375 --> 00:51:30.208
No.

627
00:51:31.166 --> 00:51:32.083
No.

628
00:51:35.541 --> 00:51:36.458
No!

629
00:52:02.000 --> 00:52:04.541
THE ADVENTURES OF TINY AND BIG

630
00:52:15.125 --> 00:52:17.625
KINGDOM/PALACE
MEANING?

631
00:52:22.916 --> 00:52:26.458
HOME!

632
00:52:42.083 --> 00:52:44.083
-He's a robot?
-No.

633
00:52:44.166 --> 00:52:48.541
He's a Zen master who uses his skills
to manipulate his physical self.

634
00:52:48.625 --> 00:52:49.625
Okay.

635
00:52:52.000 --> 00:52:53.083
-Hi.
-Good morning.

636
00:52:55.458 --> 00:52:57.000
-Hey.
-Any news?

637
00:52:59.583 --> 00:53:02.125
We're tracking it with a drone.

638
00:53:03.500 --> 00:53:05.125
It's stopped in a gorge.

639
00:53:07.083 --> 00:53:07.916
And?

640
00:53:09.875 --> 00:53:11.458
They're preparing an air strike.

641
00:53:13.083 --> 00:53:14.541
Another attack?

642
00:53:14.625 --> 00:53:15.500
Nora.

643
00:53:16.958 --> 00:53:18.708
We're all at a loss.

644
00:53:19.500 --> 00:53:20.625
I mean…

645
00:53:22.125 --> 00:53:23.875
What are we up against here?

646
00:53:25.666 --> 00:53:28.500
I don't know what I saw

647
00:53:28.583 --> 00:53:30.333
or what I believe.

648
00:53:32.333 --> 00:53:33.250
What if…

649
00:53:34.416 --> 00:53:35.708
What if what?

650
00:53:36.875 --> 00:53:40.333
What if… there's some truth
to the fairy tales

651
00:53:40.416 --> 00:53:41.250
Hey.

652
00:53:42.416 --> 00:53:45.250
You've been through a lot
in the last 24 hours.

653
00:53:45.333 --> 00:53:46.500
-I--
-The mistake.

654
00:53:47.416 --> 00:53:48.250
What?

655
00:53:48.833 --> 00:53:51.541
Your dad said

656
00:53:51.625 --> 00:53:54.750
that Kittelsen made a deliberate mistake
in the drawing.

657
00:53:55.458 --> 00:53:57.458
Trolls can't survive in the sun.

658
00:53:57.541 --> 00:53:58.791
But look.

659
00:53:58.875 --> 00:54:01.083
He's strolling around in broad daylight.

660
00:54:01.166 --> 00:54:03.416
So Kittelsen was right.

661
00:54:04.000 --> 00:54:04.958
What do you mean?

662
00:54:06.250 --> 00:54:08.291
We've seen it during the day.

663
00:54:08.375 --> 00:54:11.750
What other rules do we know
from the fairy tales?

664
00:54:11.833 --> 00:54:12.791
Seriously?

665
00:54:12.875 --> 00:54:15.833
-Okay, forget sunlight.
-I mean…

666
00:54:15.916 --> 00:54:18.750
We grew up with them. Come on, Andreas.

667
00:54:18.833 --> 00:54:21.166
You shouldn't feed them after midnight.

668
00:54:21.250 --> 00:54:24.041
-Are you actually saying it's a real--
-Crosses?

669
00:54:24.125 --> 00:54:25.416
That's vampires.

670
00:54:25.500 --> 00:54:27.875
Crosses. That's religion.

671
00:54:29.833 --> 00:54:31.083
The soldier.

672
00:54:32.458 --> 00:54:33.625
Look at this.

673
00:54:33.708 --> 00:54:35.375
"It smells like Christian blood."

674
00:54:36.666 --> 00:54:38.458
The Christianization of Norway.

675
00:54:46.833 --> 00:54:49.375
<i>What you're suggesting is insane.</i>

676
00:54:49.458 --> 00:54:51.458
<i>Completely insane.</i>

677
00:54:51.541 --> 00:54:54.416
<i>-We can't act on such absurd--</i>
-Superstition?

678
00:54:54.916 --> 00:54:56.416
Fiction?

679
00:54:56.500 --> 00:54:58.291
<i>Come on. Seriously?</i>

680
00:54:58.916 --> 00:55:00.291
The old myths

681
00:55:00.375 --> 00:55:04.333
speak of trolls
hurling boulders at churches.

682
00:55:04.416 --> 00:55:06.291
They couldn't stand the bells.

683
00:55:07.291 --> 00:55:09.041
<i>This just keeps getting better.</i>

684
00:55:10.666 --> 00:55:12.125
<i>What's your opinion, Andreas?</i>

685
00:55:14.416 --> 00:55:15.541
Prime Minister.

686
00:55:16.916 --> 00:55:20.625
From what we've seen so far,
we're unable to find--

687
00:55:20.708 --> 00:55:21.625
General.

688
00:55:23.666 --> 00:55:25.583
Permission to speak?

689
00:55:26.250 --> 00:55:27.333
<i>Go ahead, Captain.</i>

690
00:55:27.833 --> 00:55:31.708
We're facing an enemy
unlike any we've faced before.

691
00:55:32.333 --> 00:55:33.916
Our modern weapons

692
00:55:34.916 --> 00:55:36.000
have no effect.

693
00:55:37.000 --> 00:55:38.916
I believe Professor Tidemann is right.

694
00:55:41.375 --> 00:55:43.250
We have to think outside the box.

695
00:55:44.375 --> 00:55:45.625
<i>Prime Minister.</i>

696
00:55:45.708 --> 00:55:49.166
<i>Tidemann's idea is a radical one.</i>

697
00:55:49.250 --> 00:55:51.666
<i>But if there's anything</i>
<i>Captain Holm and I know,</i>

698
00:55:51.750 --> 00:55:55.041
<i>it's that extreme circumstances</i>

699
00:55:55.791 --> 00:55:57.250
<i>require extreme measures.</i>

700
00:55:57.833 --> 00:55:58.666
<i>Very well.</i>

701
00:55:59.333 --> 00:56:01.125
<i>-Go ahead.</i>
<i>-Oh my God.</i>

702
00:56:10.000 --> 00:56:12.791
If we evacuate now, we'll create panic.

703
00:56:12.875 --> 00:56:14.541
Yes, but we need a plan.

704
00:56:14.625 --> 00:56:15.666
We can't.

705
00:56:15.750 --> 00:56:16.875
It's…

706
00:56:16.958 --> 00:56:18.875
It's moving southeast.

707
00:56:20.625 --> 00:56:22.208
What's in that direction?

708
00:56:23.000 --> 00:56:26.083
HUNDERFOSSEN FAMILY PARK
LILLEHAMMER

709
00:56:36.583 --> 00:56:37.791
Look.

710
00:56:38.416 --> 00:56:40.750
-Thank you.
-Don't run too far, Viktor.

711
00:57:03.708 --> 00:57:04.916
Viktor?

712
00:57:05.583 --> 00:57:07.833
-Klara, come here.
-What's going on?

713
00:57:28.583 --> 00:57:30.375
Thomas, what are you doing?

714
00:57:50.625 --> 00:57:52.875
Tidemann, what are you expecting
to happen?

715
00:57:52.958 --> 00:57:54.625
That it's going to crack open?

716
00:58:01.375 --> 00:58:02.500
Lovely.

717
00:58:05.666 --> 00:58:06.833
<i>This is Hocus 1.</i>

718
00:58:06.916 --> 00:58:08.916
Stay in formation. Initiating 360.

719
00:58:21.666 --> 00:58:22.875
It's working.

720
00:58:29.000 --> 00:58:31.500
This is Hocus 1. Tighten formation.

721
00:58:35.041 --> 00:58:36.291
Viktor!

722
00:58:45.750 --> 00:58:47.208
Hocus 3, incoming left!

723
00:58:50.875 --> 00:58:51.916
<i>Mayday!</i>

724
00:59:03.291 --> 00:59:04.250
Hocus 4.

725
00:59:21.958 --> 00:59:23.333
No.

726
00:59:38.500 --> 00:59:40.625
Did you see that? He saved the boy.

727
01:00:04.458 --> 01:00:06.416
<i>Could it be a Norwegian Godzilla?</i>

728
01:00:09.208 --> 01:00:11.416
<i>It was really, really scary.</i>

729
01:00:11.500 --> 01:00:14.541
<i>Extensive destruction</i>
<i>along the Gudbrandsdalen valley.</i>

730
01:00:14.625 --> 01:00:18.250
<i>Military everywhere.</i>
<i>Supposedly a monster here.</i>

731
01:00:18.333 --> 01:00:19.541
<i>Utterly devastated.</i>

732
01:00:19.625 --> 01:00:20.833
<i>…trail of destruction.</i>

733
01:00:26.333 --> 01:00:30.291
<i>If we follow these tracks, it appears</i>
<i>to be heading directly for the capital.</i>

734
01:00:32.958 --> 01:00:36.416
<i>The government has not made a statement,</i>
<i>and there is speculation</i>

735
01:00:36.500 --> 01:00:40.000
<i>as to whether this is connected</i>
<i>to the incident at Dovre yesterday.</i>

736
01:01:00.083 --> 01:01:02.125
This wasn't the desired outcome,

737
01:01:02.208 --> 01:01:05.083
but we're onto something here.

738
01:01:05.708 --> 01:01:07.500
The bells had an effect.

739
01:01:07.583 --> 01:01:10.208
-We're going to have to face reality.
-Yes.

740
01:01:10.291 --> 01:01:12.916
There's a killing machine
headed towards the capital.

741
01:01:13.000 --> 01:01:14.708
I know we don't have much time,

742
01:01:14.791 --> 01:01:18.791
but if we can find out
what we're dealing with

743
01:01:18.875 --> 01:01:20.541
and why it's heading here,

744
01:01:20.625 --> 01:01:22.708
we can find a way to stop it.

745
01:01:22.791 --> 01:01:24.416
So what do you think it is?

746
01:01:27.125 --> 01:01:28.916
If you open your mind,

747
01:01:30.833 --> 01:01:32.083
what do you believe it is?

748
01:01:32.166 --> 01:01:33.208
A threat.

749
01:01:34.500 --> 01:01:37.666
That's all I need to know.
A threat that must be forcibly stopped.

750
01:01:37.750 --> 01:01:39.916
-No hocus-pocus.
-Prime Minister.

751
01:01:43.541 --> 01:01:46.041
Unbelievable doesn't mean impossible.

752
01:01:50.916 --> 01:01:54.250
Thank you for your contribution,
Professor Tidemann.

753
01:02:01.583 --> 01:02:02.541
Tidemann.

754
01:02:12.875 --> 01:02:14.041
I…

755
01:02:26.625 --> 01:02:27.458
Nora?

756
01:02:31.750 --> 01:02:33.583
No one could have done a better job.

757
01:02:36.375 --> 01:02:39.166
I think they're making a mistake.
I want you to know that.

758
01:02:40.833 --> 01:02:41.833
Captain Kris.

759
01:02:44.375 --> 01:02:47.833
And if there's anything I can do,
let me know.

760
01:02:50.041 --> 01:02:52.166
As long as it doesn't involve
church bells.

761
01:02:53.166 --> 01:02:54.500
I'll try to remember that.

762
01:02:55.291 --> 01:02:58.208
We'll barricade all routes
into the city from the northeast.

763
01:02:58.291 --> 01:03:00.041
What if it breaks through?

764
01:03:00.125 --> 01:03:02.458
There are alternatives, of course.

765
01:03:02.541 --> 01:03:03.708
No.

766
01:03:03.791 --> 01:03:05.916
No? What are you talking about?

767
01:03:06.000 --> 01:03:09.208
We have at our disposal

768
01:03:10.125 --> 01:03:11.291
certain missiles

769
01:03:11.833 --> 01:03:14.000
that aren't authorized for use. Yet.

770
01:03:14.583 --> 01:03:17.250
What you're suggesting
goes against everything

771
01:03:17.333 --> 01:03:19.000
the Armed Forces stand for.

772
01:03:19.083 --> 01:03:21.750
Not to mention
the catastrophic damage it would cause.

773
01:03:21.833 --> 01:03:23.958
What kind of weapon are we talking about?

774
01:03:24.041 --> 01:03:25.958
Why wasn't I informed?

775
01:03:26.041 --> 01:03:27.458
We're working on--

776
01:03:27.541 --> 01:03:29.750
You can't possibly consider this.

777
01:03:29.833 --> 01:03:32.791
Why is he still here?

778
01:03:34.750 --> 01:03:35.833
Jeez.

779
01:03:35.916 --> 01:03:38.791
Would you leave the room for a moment,
Andreas?

780
01:03:53.291 --> 01:03:55.541
You can consider this my retirement.

781
01:04:10.541 --> 01:04:11.375
Excuse me.

782
01:04:17.666 --> 01:04:18.500
Nora!

783
01:04:20.416 --> 01:04:22.666
-I'll take it from here.
-What are you doing?

784
01:04:23.166 --> 01:04:25.541
You forgot Tobias's backpack.

785
01:04:26.416 --> 01:04:28.208
Come with me. I'll drive.

786
01:04:33.000 --> 01:04:34.250
What's going on?

787
01:04:34.333 --> 01:04:35.791
They're evacuating Oslo.

788
01:04:49.875 --> 01:04:51.166
My fellow citizens.

789
01:04:53.916 --> 01:04:57.000
Many of you have heard the news
from the Dovre Mountains

790
01:04:57.083 --> 01:05:00.958
<i>and seen the incredible footage</i>
<i>from Gudbrandsdalen.</i>

791
01:05:02.291 --> 01:05:05.958
You may have thought
that these were special effects.

792
01:05:06.791 --> 01:05:08.625
But this is not a fairy tale.

793
01:05:08.708 --> 01:05:11.000
This is real.

794
01:05:11.708 --> 01:05:16.000
<i>Norway has always been prepared</i>
<i>to deal with a major crisis.</i>

795
01:05:16.708 --> 01:05:20.875
But nothing could have prepared us
for what we are facing now.

796
01:05:22.458 --> 01:05:26.458
<i>A creature unknown to science</i>

797
01:05:27.541 --> 01:05:29.458
<i>has risen from the deep.</i>

798
01:05:31.000 --> 01:05:33.125
<i>History will have to be rewritten.</i>

799
01:05:34.625 --> 01:05:37.375
<i>But first we need to secure our people</i>,

800
01:05:37.958 --> 01:05:39.250
<i>our country.</i>

801
01:05:39.916 --> 01:05:42.916
<i>Since the first reports came in</i>
<i>from Dovre yesterday morning,</i>

802
01:05:43.458 --> 01:05:46.791
<i>the government, the armed forces,</i>
<i>and our top scientists</i>

803
01:05:46.875 --> 01:05:50.416
<i>have done their best</i>
<i>to contain the situation.</i>

804
01:05:53.583 --> 01:05:56.625
It's with a heavy heart
that I have to inform you

805
01:05:56.708 --> 01:05:59.750
that our efforts have so far failed.

806
01:06:01.791 --> 01:06:05.041
<i>We believe it is necessary</i>
<i>to implement additional measures</i>

807
01:06:05.125 --> 01:06:08.375
<i>to prevent further loss of human life.</i>

808
01:06:10.916 --> 01:06:12.416
<i>I urge you all</i>

809
01:06:12.500 --> 01:06:15.250
<i>to take this as seriously</i>

810
01:06:15.333 --> 01:06:17.916
<i>as the government and parliament do.</i>

811
01:06:19.250 --> 01:06:21.666
<i>I am declaring a state of emergency</i>

812
01:06:22.250 --> 01:06:27.125
<i>and ordering the immediate evacuation</i>
<i>of Oslo and all surrounding areas.</i>

813
01:06:29.166 --> 01:06:31.000
<i>We have overcome crises in our past.</i>

814
01:06:31.875 --> 01:06:34.916
<i>We stood united in fellowship.</i>
<i>We looked out for one another.</i>

815
01:06:36.708 --> 01:06:39.541
<i>From the bottom of my heart,</i>
<i>I now ask this of you.</i>

816
01:06:41.375 --> 01:06:42.666
Take care of each other.

817
01:06:43.750 --> 01:06:45.083
And God bless…

818
01:06:48.166 --> 01:06:49.583
our dear fatherland.

819
01:06:54.166 --> 01:06:55.333
"Retirement."

820
01:06:56.583 --> 01:06:57.916
I said "retirement."

821
01:06:59.125 --> 01:07:01.333
That sounds like
I'm getting too old to work.

822
01:07:03.750 --> 01:07:06.541
Why couldn't I have said, "I quit,"
like normal people?

823
01:07:07.208 --> 01:07:09.125
What a bonehead.

824
01:07:13.125 --> 01:07:14.166
Sinding?

825
01:07:14.250 --> 01:07:16.750
Yes, but I don't know what it means.

826
01:07:16.833 --> 01:07:18.750
He mentions it several times.

827
01:07:18.833 --> 01:07:21.375
"Sinding? Gatekeeper."

828
01:07:21.458 --> 01:07:23.416
Maybe he means Rikard Sinding.

829
01:07:24.333 --> 01:07:27.375
-Who's that?
-Lord Chamberlain at the Royal Palace.

830
01:07:29.541 --> 01:07:34.250
I've met Rikard during my numerous visits
to the palace.

831
01:07:35.125 --> 01:07:37.458
SINDING?
KINGDOM/PALACE? MEANING?

832
01:07:39.083 --> 01:07:39.958
The palace.

833
01:07:41.041 --> 01:07:43.500
Home. The king.

834
01:07:45.833 --> 01:07:48.208
-What is it?
-We have to turn around.

835
01:07:48.291 --> 01:07:49.875
We have to go to the palace.

836
01:07:55.666 --> 01:07:57.750
Sorry! Prime Minister's Office!

837
01:08:06.375 --> 01:08:09.250
THE ROYAL PALACE
OSLO

838
01:08:11.333 --> 01:08:12.250
Stop!

839
01:08:15.708 --> 01:08:17.541
-Freeze!
-We come in peace.

840
01:08:17.625 --> 01:08:20.583
Hands above your head!
Turn around and walk back to the car.

841
01:08:20.666 --> 01:08:22.750
-We're from the PM's Office.
-Do it!

842
01:08:22.833 --> 01:08:24.708
We don't have time for this.

843
01:08:24.791 --> 01:08:26.166
Final warning!

844
01:08:26.250 --> 01:08:27.458
Or maybe we do.

845
01:08:27.541 --> 01:08:29.500
Walk back towards the car!

846
01:08:29.583 --> 01:08:30.916
Stand down, gentlemen.

847
01:08:32.458 --> 01:08:33.416
Stand down.

848
01:08:35.416 --> 01:08:37.791
Sinding. It's me, Isaksen.

849
01:08:39.375 --> 01:08:41.083
Advisor to Prime Minister Moberg.

850
01:08:41.833 --> 01:08:44.583
I assumed someone
would eventually show up.

851
01:08:45.333 --> 01:08:49.291
No surprise it was a Tidemann.

852
01:08:56.958 --> 01:08:58.625
You have Tobias's eyes.

853
01:08:59.625 --> 01:09:01.791
I had great respect for your father.

854
01:09:02.500 --> 01:09:04.958
He despised me, but…

855
01:09:06.083 --> 01:09:07.541
Tobias was a good man.

856
01:09:08.125 --> 01:09:09.875
Stubborn as a mule.

857
01:09:13.916 --> 01:09:17.041
I can count on one hand
the number of living people

858
01:09:17.125 --> 01:09:20.000
who've seen what you're about to see.

859
01:09:29.250 --> 01:09:31.958
I would normally insist

860
01:09:32.833 --> 01:09:34.833
that ladies go first.

861
01:09:37.458 --> 01:09:38.791
I won't tell anyone.

862
01:09:39.625 --> 01:09:43.916
It was once believed
that it would bring good luck

863
01:09:44.000 --> 01:09:47.958
to build a royal palace
on top of another king's home.

864
01:09:48.666 --> 01:09:53.875
It was almost discovered in the 1920s
during construction of the subway.

865
01:09:53.958 --> 01:09:57.083
And again 12 years ago.

866
01:09:58.125 --> 01:09:59.500
What did you say?

867
01:09:59.583 --> 01:10:01.916
What we did to Tobias has weighed on me.

868
01:10:02.000 --> 01:10:04.208
But it had to be done. I'm sorry.

869
01:10:04.291 --> 01:10:08.458
You ruin the life of an innocent man,
and all you can say is "sorry"?

870
01:10:08.541 --> 01:10:11.041
I hope this will give you some answers.

871
01:10:17.125 --> 01:10:19.750
This was the home of the Mountain King.

872
01:10:24.416 --> 01:10:25.666
My God.

873
01:10:27.208 --> 01:10:30.333
During the Christianization of Norway,
Saint Olaf rid the land

874
01:10:30.416 --> 01:10:32.666
of all things
incompatible with the new faith.

875
01:10:34.708 --> 01:10:37.375
He knew that nothing,

876
01:10:37.458 --> 01:10:38.833
not even for trolls,

877
01:10:38.916 --> 01:10:42.375
is more precious than family.

878
01:10:44.250 --> 01:10:45.375
What happened to them?

879
01:10:46.916 --> 01:10:49.291
It was a massacre.

880
01:10:51.083 --> 01:10:54.250
But they spared
one of the Mountain King's offspring

881
01:10:54.333 --> 01:10:58.500
and used it to lure him
back into darkness.

882
01:10:59.958 --> 01:11:02.458
Deep into the Dovre Mountains.

883
01:11:03.250 --> 01:11:05.500
Lock him up and leave him to die.

884
01:11:14.625 --> 01:11:16.041
So my father was right.

885
01:11:17.375 --> 01:11:19.666
The King is trying
to get back to his castle.

886
01:11:20.375 --> 01:11:21.583
He wants to go home.

887
01:11:35.500 --> 01:11:36.500
Andreas.

888
01:11:37.333 --> 01:11:38.166
Look.

889
01:11:43.000 --> 01:11:44.541
"From darkness they rose."

890
01:11:45.125 --> 01:11:46.666
"And in sunlight they froze."

891
01:11:47.833 --> 01:11:50.500
That can't be right.
We've seen him in broad daylight.

892
01:11:51.083 --> 01:11:55.291
We've seen him during the day,
but have we seen him in direct sunlight?

893
01:11:55.375 --> 01:11:57.875
How does that help?
We can't control the sun.

894
01:12:00.291 --> 01:12:02.625
What's the biggest car
you have at the palace?

895
01:12:26.500 --> 01:12:27.541
Open fire.

896
01:12:34.125 --> 01:12:37.416
Her Royal Highness the Queen's
personal favorite.

897
01:12:39.291 --> 01:12:40.125
Okay.

898
01:12:41.416 --> 01:12:42.666
We've got wheels.

899
01:12:44.375 --> 01:12:45.791
Now we need muscle.

900
01:12:55.125 --> 01:12:56.041
Tidemann.

901
01:12:58.458 --> 01:12:59.500
What?

902
01:13:00.916 --> 01:13:01.833
A plan?

903
01:13:12.875 --> 01:13:14.125
It will destroy us.

904
01:13:15.916 --> 01:13:16.958
All of Oslo.

905
01:13:19.708 --> 01:13:22.041
The Prime Minister
needs to make a decision.

906
01:13:24.916 --> 01:13:26.125
Do what has to be done.

907
01:13:29.291 --> 01:13:32.041
Terminate it before it terminates us.

908
01:13:33.333 --> 01:13:36.083
We can't do it
in the middle of Karl Johan Street,

909
01:13:36.166 --> 01:13:39.250
but we can lure him away
towards Holmenkollen.

910
01:13:39.333 --> 01:13:40.333
Too far away.

911
01:13:40.416 --> 01:13:43.541
We need somewhere closer, an easier route.

912
01:13:46.125 --> 01:13:47.125
Ekeberg.

913
01:13:47.208 --> 01:13:49.833
I'll ask some buddies from the Home Guard.

914
01:13:49.916 --> 01:13:53.250
But where are we gonna get that number of…

915
01:13:57.375 --> 01:13:58.708
I've got an idea.

916
01:14:17.750 --> 01:14:18.750
Code as follows.

917
01:14:19.541 --> 01:14:20.958
<i>One, six, zero, three,</i>

918
01:14:21.583 --> 01:14:22.833
<i>seven, six, nine, nine,</i>

919
01:14:23.333 --> 01:14:25.500
<i>three, six, five, six, seven.</i>

920
01:14:27.000 --> 01:14:28.208
Code as follows.

921
01:14:28.291 --> 01:14:31.125
One, seven, eight, seven,

922
01:14:31.208 --> 01:14:32.833
six, eight, three…

923
01:14:38.666 --> 01:14:40.208
<i>Code verified.</i>

924
01:14:41.791 --> 01:14:43.625
<i>Commencing mission.</i>

925
01:14:48.958 --> 01:14:50.333
Get in.

926
01:14:51.125 --> 01:14:53.083
Sigmeister, give me some good news.

927
01:14:53.166 --> 01:14:56.041
The barricades have been breached.
They're bombing Oslo.

928
01:14:56.125 --> 01:14:57.791
-Not good.
-What does that mean?

929
01:14:57.875 --> 01:14:59.750
So long, Oslo.

930
01:14:59.833 --> 01:15:03.333
-We need to buy more time.
-Can't you just hack the system?

931
01:15:03.416 --> 01:15:06.000
How hard can it be
to hack a military network

932
01:15:06.083 --> 01:15:08.583
and override a high-tech fighter?

933
01:15:09.166 --> 01:15:12.125
-Sorry! I'm just trying to--
-No. Seriously.

934
01:15:12.208 --> 01:15:13.958
How hard can it be?

935
01:15:15.833 --> 01:15:16.875
I see.

936
01:15:18.333 --> 01:15:19.666
WELCOME TO OSLO

937
01:15:38.500 --> 01:15:40.833
It's a lot to take in. Just do it later.

938
01:15:40.916 --> 01:15:43.416
EKEBERG FIELDS
OSLO

939
01:16:23.958 --> 01:16:24.916
All set.

940
01:16:30.333 --> 01:16:31.625
Come on.

941
01:16:37.750 --> 01:16:39.916
Target is approaching the city center.

942
01:16:41.333 --> 01:16:43.125
<i>HQ, this is Raven 4.</i>

943
01:16:43.208 --> 01:16:45.000
<i>Confirming course for Oslo.</i>

944
01:16:50.458 --> 01:16:51.916
TARGET: ØRLAND_AIRPORT

945
01:17:04.333 --> 01:17:05.166
Amir!

946
01:17:05.250 --> 01:17:07.000
<i>Salaam alaikum.</i>

947
01:17:07.083 --> 01:17:08.416
<i>Alaikum salaam, </i>brother.

948
01:17:10.166 --> 01:17:12.041
-What a job.
<i>-</i>Did you recruit anyone?

949
01:17:12.125 --> 01:17:13.166
The cavalry?

950
01:17:21.916 --> 01:17:23.250
If we survive this,

951
01:17:24.000 --> 01:17:26.125
I owe you a Pepsi Max and a Toblerone.

952
01:17:33.916 --> 01:17:37.041
If your hacker friend fails now…

953
01:17:37.125 --> 01:17:39.500
Siggy is the Spock to my Captain Kirk.

954
01:17:41.458 --> 01:17:43.000
Siggy has never failed.

955
01:17:43.083 --> 01:17:45.250
She doesn't know how to.

956
01:17:52.041 --> 01:17:56.166
<i>This is Raven 4.</i>
<i>Target acquired. Awaiting orders.</i>

957
01:17:57.000 --> 01:17:58.083
Engage.

958
01:17:58.166 --> 01:17:59.791
Blow it to smithereens.

959
01:17:59.875 --> 01:18:00.833
<i>Copy.</i>

960
01:18:02.458 --> 01:18:04.500
<i>Firing missile in five,</i>

961
01:18:05.583 --> 01:18:06.416
<i>four,</i>

962
01:18:07.125 --> 01:18:08.750
<i>three, two,</i>

963
01:18:09.541 --> 01:18:10.541
<i>one…</i>

964
01:18:12.416 --> 01:18:15.750
<i>No. System failure. What the…</i>

965
01:18:15.833 --> 01:18:16.833
Jackpot!

966
01:18:23.625 --> 01:18:24.458
Siggy.

967
01:18:26.583 --> 01:18:27.500
Okay.

968
01:18:27.583 --> 01:18:29.041
Why's nothing happening?

969
01:18:29.541 --> 01:18:31.125
Why is nothing happening?

970
01:18:31.208 --> 01:18:33.666
I can't access the control panel.

971
01:18:33.750 --> 01:18:35.916
Is the network connection down?

972
01:18:43.333 --> 01:18:44.916
What if it doesn't work?

973
01:18:49.125 --> 01:18:50.708
What if I'm just like my Dad?

974
01:18:51.458 --> 01:18:52.666
Completely crazy.

975
01:18:52.750 --> 01:18:56.375
Yeah, and in a crazy world,
only the crazy are sane.

976
01:18:57.875 --> 01:19:00.958
And no one is as bonkers as you,
Nora Tidemann.

977
01:19:03.833 --> 01:19:04.833
Thank you.

978
01:19:06.416 --> 01:19:07.833
I think.

979
01:19:11.750 --> 01:19:12.708
Okay, Andreas.

980
01:19:14.583 --> 01:19:16.083
Buckle up.

981
01:19:31.958 --> 01:19:33.458
Dear God.

982
01:19:40.916 --> 01:19:41.833
Hey ho.

983
01:20:15.208 --> 01:20:16.208
Now!

984
01:20:29.250 --> 01:20:31.375
He's coming! Go!

985
01:20:46.708 --> 01:20:47.833
-Status?
-On our way.

986
01:20:47.916 --> 01:20:49.166
<i>No.</i>

987
01:20:51.166 --> 01:20:52.291
<i>We need more time.</i>

988
01:20:52.375 --> 01:20:54.791
We don't have more time.
We'll be there in 15.

989
01:20:58.750 --> 01:20:59.750
Make that ten.

990
01:21:00.291 --> 01:21:01.291
No, Nora…

991
01:21:04.583 --> 01:21:05.458
We're not ready.

992
01:21:13.250 --> 01:21:14.416
Soldiers!

993
01:21:16.083 --> 01:21:17.500
Gather round!

994
01:21:17.583 --> 01:21:18.416
Come on!

995
01:21:23.125 --> 01:21:25.875
We have an incoming threat
from that direction.

996
01:21:25.958 --> 01:21:28.208
ETA ten minutes.

997
01:21:30.333 --> 01:21:32.125
What's about to come over that hill

998
01:21:32.208 --> 01:21:35.208
is unlike anything you've ever faced.

999
01:21:36.250 --> 01:21:37.708
I'll be honest with you.

1000
01:21:39.541 --> 01:21:42.583
There's a good chance
this operation won't go our way.

1001
01:21:43.708 --> 01:21:45.083
But ask yourself this.

1002
01:21:47.125 --> 01:21:48.083
Who are we

1003
01:21:48.750 --> 01:21:50.625
if we give up without a fight?

1004
01:21:51.583 --> 01:21:54.750
Who are we
if we let fear get the better of us?

1005
01:21:54.833 --> 01:21:58.041
Who are we
if we let something trample all over us?

1006
01:21:58.125 --> 01:22:00.041
Without first saying,

1007
01:22:00.125 --> 01:22:03.166
"Not here! Not on our watch!"

1008
01:22:10.500 --> 01:22:12.041
The bridge is closed.

1009
01:22:18.375 --> 01:22:20.333
No! The head!

1010
01:22:20.416 --> 01:22:22.000
We've lost the head!

1011
01:23:16.041 --> 01:23:17.541
Hey there, beautiful.

1012
01:23:47.583 --> 01:23:48.583
Lonely.

1013
01:23:52.750 --> 01:23:54.291
All alone in the world.

1014
01:23:56.666 --> 01:23:59.458
It's like the tale
about the Three Billy Goats Gruff.

1015
01:24:01.666 --> 01:24:05.375
The biggest goat isn't coming.
If you're going to drive, now's the time.

1016
01:24:57.000 --> 01:24:58.000
Still no connection?

1017
01:24:58.083 --> 01:25:00.791
Something's blocking the system
from the inside.

1018
01:25:05.458 --> 01:25:06.791
What are you doing?

1019
01:25:07.625 --> 01:25:12.583
I'm glad you're here.
Someone's taken control of my computer.

1020
01:25:12.666 --> 01:25:16.916
I opened an email
from this prince in Nigeria.

1021
01:25:22.541 --> 01:25:23.666
Do you realize

1022
01:25:24.625 --> 01:25:26.041
what you've done?

1023
01:25:33.375 --> 01:25:34.625
<i>This is Raven 4.</i>

1024
01:25:34.708 --> 01:25:36.500
<i>System online. Awaiting new orders.</i>

1025
01:25:36.583 --> 01:25:38.583
You're still authorized to engage.

1026
01:25:39.416 --> 01:25:40.250
<i>Copy.</i>

1027
01:25:41.000 --> 01:25:42.458
Let's finish this.

1028
01:25:49.541 --> 01:25:50.875
Go!

1029
01:26:02.875 --> 01:26:03.875
We have to jump!

1030
01:26:07.208 --> 01:26:08.833
Get ready!

1031
01:26:11.916 --> 01:26:13.250
Now!

1032
01:26:29.833 --> 01:26:31.208
Nora!

1033
01:26:39.125 --> 01:26:41.000
-Amir, are we ready?
-Not yet.

1034
01:26:47.416 --> 01:26:48.333
Nora!

1035
01:26:54.500 --> 01:26:55.666
Go!

1036
01:27:02.666 --> 01:27:03.916
Nora! Come on.

1037
01:27:14.958 --> 01:27:17.875
<i>Raven 4 locked on target. Weapon armed.</i>

1038
01:27:42.458 --> 01:27:44.250
<i>Civilians spotted.</i>

1039
01:27:44.333 --> 01:27:46.375
<i>I repeat, civilians spotted.</i>

1040
01:27:46.458 --> 01:27:48.000
-Abort.
<i>-</i>Abort.

1041
01:27:48.083 --> 01:27:49.166
No.

1042
01:27:49.791 --> 01:27:50.625
<i>Abort.</i>

1043
01:27:50.708 --> 01:27:52.083
No, for God's sake.

1044
01:27:52.958 --> 01:27:54.583
No. Blow it up.

1045
01:27:54.666 --> 01:27:55.958
Destroy that monster!

1046
01:27:59.750 --> 01:28:01.083
Blow it up, dammit!

1047
01:28:01.166 --> 01:28:02.541
Destroy it!

1048
01:28:03.666 --> 01:28:05.333
I repeat, abort.

1049
01:28:05.833 --> 01:28:06.916
Aborting mission.

1050
01:28:23.875 --> 01:28:25.333
You're a genius!

1051
01:28:59.083 --> 01:29:00.625
This is wrong.

1052
01:29:01.291 --> 01:29:02.416
What?

1053
01:29:03.000 --> 01:29:05.916
It's working.

1054
01:29:06.541 --> 01:29:07.833
We're killing it.

1055
01:29:07.916 --> 01:29:09.125
Wasn't that the plan?

1056
01:29:15.958 --> 01:29:17.750
-Not like this.
-Nora?

1057
01:29:19.541 --> 01:29:20.708
Nora Tidemann!

1058
01:29:41.333 --> 01:29:43.000
You have to stop them.

1059
01:29:43.750 --> 01:29:44.583
Stop!

1060
01:29:45.958 --> 01:29:47.083
You have to go!

1061
01:29:48.708 --> 01:29:50.750
Please. Get away from here!

1062
01:29:51.500 --> 01:29:52.583
Amir.

1063
01:29:52.666 --> 01:29:53.708
Easy.

1064
01:29:54.208 --> 01:29:55.291
Just…

1065
01:29:59.125 --> 01:30:00.083
Just…

1066
01:30:00.875 --> 01:30:02.916
Go back to the mountains!

1067
01:30:04.000 --> 01:30:05.000
Please.

1068
01:30:06.416 --> 01:30:07.875
Go where you're safe.

1069
01:30:14.708 --> 01:30:16.791
We won't come after you. Just go.

1070
01:32:12.250 --> 01:32:14.708
No more Norway Cup here, that's for sure.

1071
01:32:24.875 --> 01:32:25.958
-Bro.
-Bro.

1072
01:32:39.958 --> 01:32:41.291
What do you think?

1073
01:32:43.125 --> 01:32:44.166
"Dovre Hill"?

1074
01:32:49.583 --> 01:32:50.791
"Tidemann Rise"?

1075
01:32:53.291 --> 01:32:54.750
Maybe "Troll Knoll"?

1076
01:32:59.000 --> 01:33:00.250
"Tobias Rock."

1077
01:33:01.541 --> 01:33:02.416
Maybe.

1078
01:33:37.875 --> 01:33:39.291
The black eye suits you.

1079
01:33:43.375 --> 01:33:44.375
Professor Tidemann.

1080
01:33:47.250 --> 01:33:48.666
I don't know what to say.

1081
01:33:59.458 --> 01:34:00.875
Prime Minister,

1082
01:34:00.958 --> 01:34:04.500
I'd just like to make it clear
that I'm not retiring.

1083
01:34:04.583 --> 01:34:06.875
I only quit this job.

1084
01:34:10.333 --> 01:34:12.041
Berit, I'm going to be a writer!

1085
01:34:22.500 --> 01:34:24.458
Think there are more of them out there?

1086
01:34:25.000 --> 01:34:27.041
Somewhere deep down in a cave.

1087
01:41:27.583 --> 01:41:30.333
Subtitle translation by:
Ekaterina Pliassova
